On May 5, 2004, at 8:05, Rhyotte wrote:

> This whole thing is getting so far outta sight it is crazy. What is 
> wrong with them simply accrediting you and the Reiser Team??????? I 
> believe I have seen you say that Credits at install time would be fine 
> right? @ the rest of you: What is wrong with that??

Just to (hopefully) clarify this situation a little... here is the 
problem in a nutshell.

Debians position is: We have no problem with attribution, but if we are 
forced to attribute in a specific manner that is not, and will not be 
acceptable.

Han's position is: That's cool, problem is that not everyone is so 
noble, and my license is trying to ensure that those who would not be 
so noble are forced to fairly attribute.

Debians counter position: Hmm. There is a problem then, we cannot 
accept a discriminatory license, so it cannot be fixed "only for us", 
and we cannot accept a license the restricts the modification of the 
code.

(I know someone will correct me if I have misstated those positions)

> In my opinion you all really need to drop the silly and counter 
> productive argument. Act like adults, make an agreement then shake 
> hands and be friends again.

What pray tell do you think they are doing, they are trying to find a 
middle ground that they can both agree on. Well mostly, there is also 
some flameage going on, but most of it was trying to describe where the 
middle ground might lie. So far, they have not been able to really 
agree on where that middle ground is.

> Sheesh, SOME of us would like to see Reiser4 out in the public as a 
> full release!!

As do we all... But that doesn't mean that all other issues become 
trivial and non-sensical.

Cheers,
Paul

